#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""P1.1 — Within-group 80/20 pixel split experiment.

Answers: "Is the spatial logic of designation learnable at all?"

Setup:
  - Load test expansion groups (2017-2024) with ALL pixels (no neg_ratio)
  - For each (country_id, year) group, assign 80% of pixels to train and 20% to val
  - Apply neg_ratio=100 to the 80% train portion (memory control)
  - Also load temporal train (2001-2013, neg_ratio=100) as additional signal
  - Train H6+H1b+H5 settings, early-stop on the 20% val (all pixels)
  - Report Recall@5% on the 20% val set

Expected: ~94.5% Recall@5% (confirmed on Colombia scale).

The gap between this and the temporal result (16-19%) measures temporal
non-stationarity: the model has strong feature signal but past events do
not perfectly predict future events. Both numbers belong in the paper.
"""

